      "content": "For your moot court competition, you can take the position that the expansion of executive privilege is not a necessary protection and instead poses a dangerous erosion of checks and balances. A stronger legal position would view the principle of checks and balances as essential to the functioning of a democratic system, ensuring that no single branch of government—especially the executive—wields excessive power without adequate oversight by the legislative branch. This viewpoint draws support from the framers' intent in the separation of powers and from historical instances where unchecked power has led to abuses. Emphasize the potential for executive privilege to be misused to avoid transparency and accountability, ultimately undermining public trust.",
